### Consolidated Analysis of the Draft Settlement Agreement

The draft agreement provided is a **Mutual Separation Agreement (*Överenskommelse om anställningens upphörande*)**. Under Swedish employment law, signing this document means you are voluntarily agreeing to end your contract and waiving all future legal claims against the employer under the Employment Protection Act (*Lagen om anställningsskydd* - LAS).

#### Key Provisions in Your Document

* **Notice Period & Garden Leave (*Arbetsbefrielse*):** You will be placed on paid garden leave from September 2026 until your end date in November 2026 (`2026-11-XX`). During this time, you keep your monthly base salary and benefits.


* **Income Deduction (*Avräkning* / Section 13 LAS):** If you take a new job during the notice period, your current employer will **not** deduct your new income from your regular salary, **unless** you join a competitor.


* **Severance Pay (*Avgångsvederlag*):** The company offers **2 months of base salary** as severance, payable after the final end date. This pay does **not** count toward holiday pay or occupational pension (*Tjänstepension*).


* **Return of Property vs. Garden Leave:** The agreement requires you to return all company equipment (laptop, phone subscription, keys) by late September 2026 (`2026-09-XX`), even though your employment lasts until November.


* **Re-employment Rights (*Företrädesrätt*):** You are asked to explicitly waive your preferential right to re-employment under Section 25 of LAS.


* **Final Settlement (*Slutreglering*):** Signing this releases both parties from all future financial or legal claims (including bonuses, holiday pay, and damages).



